WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:09.530
July 20, 1976: Viking 1 sends the first photograph from the surface of Mars.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:12.010
It arrived line by line.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:21.100
Franchesca's Andes look like Mars: high, dry, salty and full of sunlight. That's why she came.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.520
<v Franchesca>If life survives here, maybe it survived there.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:32.330
Mars opens a window every 26 months. Miss it, and you wait two more years.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.490
The whole country is watching.

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:44.240
A parachute tears in the test. Seven days to the window.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.360
<v Chicho>Then we sew a new one. Tonight.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:53.850
And they are not alone. On Mars, a small box on a rover made oxygen from the air:

00:00:53.890 --> 00:01:00.050
122 grams, between 2021 and 2023.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:04.280
Land. Breathe. Stay.

